[[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025817\">7040E50</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3025933\">7065C33</a> (left and right sides)</p><p>1. Undo the front screws securing the ceiling trim.</p><p>2. Slightly lower the ceiling trim.</p><p>3. Undo the screws fixing the rain sensor unit.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Once removed, the rain sensor\ncan no longer be reused and must be replaced.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>4. Move the rain sensor unit slightly.</p><p>5. Disconnect the electrical connection and recover the sensor.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Rain sensor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024338\">K85</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2004854.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p><a href=\"#/3025466\">5050B64</a> .</p>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p><a href=\"#/3025466\">5050B64</a> .</p><p>Thoroughly clean the inside of the windscreen\nby the sensor housing. Use a degreasing product.</p><p>Connect the sensor electrical connection.</p><p>Remove the protection from the jelly-like\nsurface of the new sensor, then place it in position.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>During this stage, take care not\nto touch the jelly-like surface with your hands.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"]]